    "b-ks2-src-intro": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "KNOWLEDGE SOURCES — A knowledge source is a store of raw material the knowledge graph cites into. Every "
        },
        {
          "insert": "evidence",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row and every "
        },
        {
          "insert": "link",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " carries a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "kind",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and a typed "
        },
        {
          "insert": "locator",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " that resolves to one record in one source. Sources hold records; the graph holds claims. Nothing points at a source row by foreign key — citation is by locator, one pointer mechanism across five heterogeneous sources — and reverse lookup (what stands on this record) is an indexed query on "
        },
        {
          "insert": "(kind, locator)",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Display resolves a locator into its source at read time; no content snapshot is stored on the citing row."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-ks2-src-intro",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-classes-heading": {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Two classes"
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-ks2-src-classes-heading",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-classes-table": {
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Class",
          "Sources",
          "Contract"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Archival",
            "Discord, pull requests, wiki",
            [
              {
                "insert": "Raw inputs, frozen once ingested. A new Discord export or PR import appends rows on the "
              },
              {
                "insert": "kg2-ingest",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " sync lane and gets them indexed; the wiki mirror is imported only on an explicit "
              },
              {
                "insert": "--lane wiki",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " — never implicitly, not even by "
              },
              {
                "insert": "--lane all",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": ". Existing rows never change, so a locator into an archival source cannot drift and carries no digest."
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            "Operational",
            "Attempts, code",
            [
              {
                "insert": "Attempts are the target ledger wearing its evidence hat — runs, submissions, and transcripts grow with every run and are immutable once written. Code is the active checkout: the only drifting source, and the only one whose citations carry a required "
              },
              {
                "insert": "digest",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": "."
              }
            ]
          ]
        ]
      },
      "id": "b-ks2-src-classes-table",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-standards-heading": {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Standards sit outside"
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-ks2-src-standards-heading",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-standards-body": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Standards are part of the knowledge system but outside the knowledge graph: QA-owned, deliberately authored rules with lints, injected at worker boot and enforced at the ship gate — see "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Standards",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/40-knowledge/70-standards",
              "label": "Standards"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". They are not a knowledge source, not walkable, and never citable as evidence. The "
        },
        {
          "insert": "kind",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " enum has no "
        },
        {
          "insert": "standards",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " entry, and the omission is deliberate."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-ks2-src-standards-body",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-grammar-heading": {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Locator grammar"
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-ks2-src-grammar-heading",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-grammar-body": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The grammar is closed. The resolver rejects any locator that does not match its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "kind",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "'s grammar, and rejects kind/scheme mismatches — a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "discord",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row with a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pr://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " locator never resolves. Each form's payload is the store row's primary key. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "code://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the one kind with no store row — the checkout at "
        },
        {
          "insert": "<revision>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the store, and only there does a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "digest",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " of the span text pin what was read."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-ks2-src-grammar-body",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-grammar-table": {
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Kind",
          "Grammar",
          "Resolves to"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "discord",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "insert": "discord://message/<discord_message.id>",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "insert": "One "
              },
              {
                "insert": "discord_message",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " row"
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "pr",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "insert": "pr://<pull_request.id>[/comment/<n>]",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "insert": "A "
              },
              {
                "insert": "pull_request",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " row, or one comment in its archived discussion"
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "wiki",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "insert": "wiki://<wiki_section.id>",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "insert": "One "
              },
              {
                "insert": "wiki_section",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " row; the id encodes page, section, and mirror revision"
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "attempt",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "insert": "attempt://run/<worker_run.id>[/submission/<seq>][/transcript/<span>]",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "A worker run, one of its submissions, or a span of its archived transcript"
          ],
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "code",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "insert": "code://<revision>/<path>#L<start>-L<end>",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "insert": "A line span in the checkout at "
              },
              {
                "insert": "<revision>",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": "; no store row, "
              },
              {
                "insert": "digest",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " required"
              }
            ]
          ]
        ]
      },
      "id": "b-ks2-src-grammar-table",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-search-heading": {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Search surfaces"
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-ks2-src-search-heading",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-search-body": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Every source declares a search surface: the retrieval primitives that may run against it, drawn from four families — keyword (BM25 full-text over the stated text columns), vector (semantic retrieval over embeddings of the stated chunks), structured (exact filters and joins on the row columns), and graph (deterministic code navigation, never ranked). Search indexes are derived and rebuildable from the source rows — never part of the record contract; dropping and re-deriving an index loses nothing. Embeddings are generated remotely through an embedding API ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "text-embedding-3",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " class; the provider is swappable), fanned out as concurrent requests so backfill turns around quickly; re-embedding is an index rebuild — nothing else changes."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-ks2-src-search-body",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-search-access": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The librarian is the only agent that searches these surfaces directly. Workers never query knowledge sources; what workers see arrives through worker surfaces built from facts. Which agents get which worker surfaces is deliberately deferred."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-ks2-src-search-access",
      "children": []
    },
